  "id": "opt",
  "term": "opt-",
  "definition": "Opt- refers to an optimal cue-combination account of perception, where the brain blends multiple sensory signals by giving more weight to the ones that are more reliable. In the packet, it describes a haptic size-judgment model in which touch and finger-position cues are integrated in this weighted way.",
